From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: rockchip: pm-config: Add rockchip,virtual-poweroff

A board may ask that power-off be a sleep the wake sources end, so a
remote's power key starts a box its user turned off. Describe the flag.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,pm-config.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,pm-config.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,pm-config.yaml
index b6cdf2a..0284ec4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,pm-config.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/rockchip/rockchip,pm-config.yaml
@@ -30,6 +30,13 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description: The PWM outputs that drive a regulator the firmware keeps.
 
+  rockchip,virtual-poweroff:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    enum: [0, 1]
+    description:
+      1 powers off as a sleep the wake sources end, the board then starting
+      afresh.
+
 required:
   - compatible
 
